From b364775de4afa373654099906b9b87457679bc85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenCode <rj@precisionailabs.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:25:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] ds4: DS4_POOL_GB pins the GPU pool's budget on
 unified-memory APUs

HIP's hipMemGetInfo on a Strix Halo APU reports the GTT pool rather than what the
host can actually give, and the number swings per process: the same 128 GB box
reported 48.0, 51.3 and 120.0 GB free within one afternoon, and the pool the
engine sized from it ranged 22.9 - 63 GB for the same flags. A 22.9 GB pool costs
about 10x decode speed (1766 vs 3828 of 15744 experts resident, 1.75 vs 17.9
tok/s measured), so the pool is not reproducible run to run.

DS4_POOL_GB=<GB> sets the budget the experts, weights and caches may take
together on each device, replacing the measured free memory. Unset, behaviour is
unchanged.

(cherry picked from commit 008b40fa6857fe5946978240dbcc8d4f45554f71)
(cherry picked from commit 0d1ff8f799885a1a4c9c73c8d1764e2f0b9782bf)
(cherry picked from commit c634d0d929b89832fea55fef8c4036e5bb70aef1)
---
 src/ds4/ds4_model.cu | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/ds4/ds4_model.cu b/src/ds4/ds4_model.cu
index dab13e1..f7c99cc 100644
--- a/src/ds4/ds4_model.cu
+++ b/src/ds4/ds4_model.cu
@@ -2313,6 +2313,19 @@ struct Model::Impl {
                 return false;
             }
             CK(mem_info(&d.free0, &d.total));
+            // (an APU: HIP's free swings with the host's page cache - 48 GB and 120 GB for the same process on a
+            //  128 GB Strix Halo, minutes apart - so the GPU pool and the read-ahead it sizes are not reproducible.
+            //  DS4_POOL_GB pins the budget the pool is sized from; it is what the experts, the weights and their
+            //  caches may take together, on this device.  Upstream's mem_info() measures the dedicated part; this
+            //  override stays so the placement is reproducible run to run.)
+            if (const char* v = std::getenv("DS4_POOL_GB")) {
+                const double gb = std::atof(v);
+                if (gb > 0) {
+                    std::fprintf(stderr, "ds4: CUDA%zu pool budget %.1f GB (DS4_POOL_GB; HIP reported %.1f GB free)\n",
+                                 i, gb, (double) d.free0 / 1e9);
+                    d.free0 = (size_t) (gb * 1e9);
+                }
+            }
         }
         // the groups' width: o.tp, less while the experts' blocks do not split in it (a member takes n_ff / tp of each
         // expert: the down's inputs in whole blocks - a GGUF's 256-value types split n_ff 2304 in 1, 3 or 9 parts)
